(This is not an easy task. To differentiate the interesting and the) Tj T*
(essential from the mass of routine material is, perhaps, not very) Tj T*
(difficult, but to present this segregated matter in a form that will) Tj T*
(not be monotonous is much more of a problem. The proceedings of a) Tj T*
(Committee that has been in continuous session must, when written down,) Tj T*
(partake of the nature of a diary, and to that extent be tiresome) Tj T*
(reading. We shall, therefore, have to ask the indulgence of any one) Tj T*
(who happens to look into these pages, and beg him to pass over the) Tj T*
(form for the sake of the substance. That the substance itself is of) Tj T*
(deep interest goes without saying. It was given to the Stock Exchange) Tj T*
(to play a great part in a momentous world crisis, and it must be of) Tj T*
(profound interest to know how that part was played.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Stock Exchanges are a relatively recent product of modern) Tj T*
(civilization, and like new comers in every field they are suspected) Tj T*
(and misunderstood. The most complex of all problems are economic) Tj T*
(problems, and the functions of Stock Exchanges form a most intricate) Tj T*
(part of political economy. It has, consequently, been a noticeable) Tj T*
(phenomenon in all contemporary industrial society that the activities) Tj T*
(of the stock markets have been a constant subject of agitation and) Tj T*
(legislative meddling. Most of this meddling has been based upon) Tj T*
(ignorance and misunderstanding, but in a broad view this ignorance and) Tj T*
(misunderstanding are excusable owing to the novelty and above all the) Tj T*
(great complexity of the factors at work. One of the needs of the time,) Tj T*
(therefore, is that the public, and their representatives in the) Tj T*
(Legislatures, should be enlightened as fast as possible with regard to) Tj T*
(the immensely important uses of these institutions, and to the) Tj T*
(operation of their very delicate machinery.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The World crisis of 1914 forced upon us an object lesson on the) Tj T*
(question of speculative exchanges in general which ought to be of) Tj T*
(lasting profit. For years agitators had been hard at work all over the) Tj T*
(country urging the suppression of the Cotton Exchanges, and claiming) Tj T*
(that they contained gamblers who depressed the price of the cotton) Tj T*
(growers' product. In the summer of 1914 the dreams of these agitators) Tj T*
(were realized. The Cotton Exchanges were all closed and the cotton) Tj T*
(grower was given an opportunity of testing the benefits of a situation) Tj T*
(where there was no reliable agency to appraise the value of cotton.) Tj T*
(The result may be summed up in the statement that the reopening of the) Tj T*
(Cotton Exchanges met with no opposition. A similar object lesson was) Tj T*
(furnished in the case of the Stock Exchanges. They were all closed,) Tj T*
(and for a few weeks some profound thinkers in the radical press stated) Tj T*
(that the country was showing its ability to dispense with them. When) Tj T*
(the time for their reopening came, however, there was no agitation to) Tj T*
(prevent it. On the contrary it was hailed as a sign of the resumption) Tj T*
(of normal financial conditions in the United States.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This evidence that the experience of 1914 has cast a much needed light) Tj T*
(on the public value of speculative exchanges, gives a further excuse) Tj T*
(for describing in some detail how the experience was passed through by) Tj T*
(that greatest of all these institutions, the New York Stock) Tj T*
(Exchange.) Tj T*
ET
