(CHAPTER I) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE CLOSING OF THE EXCHANGE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Stock Exchange is in the second century of its existence and in) Tj T*
(that long period of time \(long relatively to the number of years) Tj T*
(during which Stock Exchanges have been known to the world\) it has been) Tj T*
(forced to close its doors only twice. The first occasion was the great) Tj T*
(panic of 1873, the after effect of civil war when trading was) Tj T*
(suspended for ten days; the second came with the outbreak of the world) Tj T*
(War in the close of July, 1914. These two remarkable events differ) Tj T*
(profoundly in the gravity of the circumstances which brought them) Tj T*
(about. In 1873, although the financial disturbance was one of the) Tj T*
(greatest the United States has ever experienced, the trouble was) Tj T*
(mainly local and did not seriously involve the entire world. The) Tj T*
(Exchange was not closed in anticipation of a catastrophe but was) Tj T*
(obliged to shut down after the crash had taken place, in order to) Tj T*
(enable Wall Street to gather up its shattered fragments. The measure) Tj T*
(of this crisis was the ten days during which trading was suspended.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Far different from these were the circumstances surrounding July 31st,) Tj T*
(1914. On that eventful date a financial earthquake of a violence) Tj T*
(absolutely without precedent shook every great center of the) Tj T*
(civilized world, closing their markets one by one until New York, the) Tj T*
(last of all, finally suspended in order to forestall what would have) Tj T*
(surely been a ruinous collapse. The four and a half months during) Tj T*
(which this suspension continued stand to the ten days closing of 1873) Tj T*
(in a proportion which fitly illustrates the relative gravity of the) Tj T*
(two historic upheavals.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the light of these facts we are justified in asserting that the) Tj T*
(events of 1914 are the most momentous that have so far constituted the) Tj T*
(life and history of the New York Stock Exchange, and consequently that) Tj T*
(some record of, and commentary upon, these facts may be of value to) Tj T*
(the present members of that body and of interest and profit to its) Tj T*
(future members.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
