(It is in the nature of panics to be unforeseen, but the statement may) Tj T*
(be truly made that some of them can be more unforeseen than others.) Tj T*
(The panic of 1907 was preceded by anxious forebodings in the minds of) Tj T*
(many well informed people, whereas the Venezuela panic in 1895, being) Tj T*
(due to the sudden act of an individual, came out of a clear sky. To) Tj T*
(the latter class distinctively belongs the great convulsion of 1914.) Tj T*
(While the standing armies of Europe were a constant reminder of) Tj T*
(possible war, and the frequent diplomatic tension between the Great) Tj T*
(Powers cast repeated war shadows over the financial markets, the) Tj T*
(American public, at least, was entirely unprepared for a world) Tj T*
(conflagration. Up to the final moment of the launching of ultimata) Tj T*
(between the European governments no one thought it possible that all) Tj T*
(our boasted bonds of civilization were to burst over night and plunge) Tj T*
(us back into mediæval barbarism. Wall Street was therefore taken) Tj T*
(unaware, and so terrific was the rapidity with which the world passed,) Tj T*
(in the period of about a week, from the confidence of long enduring) Tj T*
(peace to the frightful realization of strife, that no time was given) Tj T*
(for men to collect their thoughts and decide how to meet the) Tj T*
(on-rushing disaster.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Added to the paralyzing effect of this unheard of speed of action,) Tj T*
(there came the disconcerting thought that the conditions produced were) Tj T*
(absolutely without precedent. Experience, the chart on which we rely) Tj T*
(to guide ourselves through troubled waters, did not exist. No world) Tj T*
(war had ever been fought under the complex conditions of modern) Tj T*
(industry and finance, and no one could, for the moment, form any) Tj T*
(reliable idea of what would happen or of what immediate action should) Tj T*
(be taken. These circumstances should be kept clearly in mind by all) Tj T*
(who wish to form a clear conception of this great emergency, and to) Tj T*
(estimate fairly the conduct of the financial community in its efforts) Tj T*
(to save the day.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The conditions on the Stock Exchange, when the storm burst, were in) Tj T*
(some respects very helpful. Speculation for several years had been at) Tj T*
(a low ebb, so that values were not inflated nor commitments extended.) Tj T*
(Had such a war broken out in 1906, with the level of prices then) Tj T*
(existing, one recoils at the thought of what might have happened.) Tj T*
(Furthermore, the unsettled business outlook due to new and untried) Tj T*
(legislation had fostered a heavy short interest in the market, thereby) Tj T*
(furnishing the best safeguard against a sudden and disastrous drop.) Tj T*
(This short interest was a leading factor in producing the) Tj T*
(extraordinary resistance of prices in New York which caused so much) Tj T*
(favorable comment during the few days before the closing. It were well) Tj T*
(if ill-informed people who deprecate short selling would note this) Tj T*
(fact.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(During the week preceding July 31st, therefore, in the face of a) Tj T*
(practical suspension of dealings in the other world markets, the New) Tj T*
(York market stood its ground wonderfully. The decline in prices,) Tj T*
(though it became violent on July 30th, showed no evidence of collapse.) Tj T*
(There was a continuous market everywhere up to the last moment, and) Tj T*
(call money was obtainable at reasonable prices. Here was a perplexing) Tj T*
ET
