(problem when the closing of foreign Bourses raised the question of how) Tj T*
(long we should strive to keep our own Exchange open.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To close the recognized public market for securities, the market which) Tj T*
(is organized and safeguarded and depended upon as a standard of) Tj T*
(values, is an undertaking of great responsibility in any community. To) Tj T*
(take this step in New York, which is one of the four preeminent) Tj T*
(financial centers of the world, involved a responsibility of a) Tj T*
(magnitude difficult adequately to estimate. Upon the continuity of) Tj T*
(this market rest the vast money loans secured by the pledge of listed) Tj T*
(securities; numberless individuals depend upon it in times of crisis) Tj T*
(to enable them to raise money rapidly by realizing on security) Tj T*
(investments and thus safeguarding other property that may be) Tj T*
(unsaleable; the possessor of ready money looks to it as the quickest) Tj T*
(and safest field in which to obtain an interest return on his funds;) Tj T*
(and the business world as a whole depends upon it as a barometer of) Tj T*
(general conditions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Add to this the fact that speculative commitments by individuals from) Tj T*
(all over the world, which have been based upon the expectation of an) Tj T*
(uninterrupted market, are left in hopeless and critical suspense if) Tj T*
(this market is suddenly removed, and it becomes apparent that to close) Tj T*
(the Exchange is manifestly to inflict far-reaching hardship upon vast) Tj T*
(numbers of people. It is also sure to be productive of much injustice.) Tj T*
(In bad times sound and solvent firms are anxious to enforce all their) Tj T*
(contracts promptly so as to protect themselves against those that are) Tj T*
(overextended; an obligatory suspension of business compels these) Tj T*
(solvent firms, in many cases, to help carry the risks of the insecure) Tj T*
(ones and deprives the provident man of the safety to which he is) Tj T*
(entitled.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When such facts as these are duly weighed by the agencies having the) Tj T*
(authority to close the stock market, it becomes clear that duty) Tj T*
(dictates a policy of hands off as long as a continuous market persists) Tj T*
(and purchasers continue to buy as the decline proceeds. This was well) Tj T*
(illustrated in the acute panic of 1907 when an enormous open market) Tj T*
(never ceased to furnish the means by which needy sellers constantly) Tj T*
(liquidated, and the possessors of savings made most profitable) Tj T*
(investments. To have closed the Exchange during that crisis--assuming) Tj T*
(it to have been possible--would have been an unmixed evil. The violent) Tj T*
(decline in prices was the natural and only remedy for a long period of) Tj T*
(over-speculation, and it would have been worse had it been) Tj T*
(artificially postponed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Considerations of this general character, up to July 30th, caused the) Tj T*
(authorities of the New York Stock Exchange to take no action, although) Tj T*
(the other world markets had all virtually suspended dealings. On July) Tj T*
(30th, the evidences of approaching panic showed themselves. An) Tj T*
(enormous business was done accompanied by very violent declines in) Tj T*
(prices, and, although money was still obtainable throughout the day,) Tj T*
(at the close of business profound uneasiness prevailed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
