(there was a very natural impatience here and there to have the) Tj T*
(Exchange reopened, while now and then a tendency became manifested to) Tj T*
(publish certain news of the day which, while interesting to the) Tj T*
(public, tended to handicap the efforts of those bent only on) Tj T*
(reassurance and calm counsel. At times it became somewhat difficult to) Tj T*
(prevent the publication of some of these matters, particularly of the) Tj T*
(prices made in the so called "gutter" market which sprang up in New) Tj T*
(Street. And yet on the whole nothing could have exceeded the fairness) Tj T*
(and the spirit of coöperation of these gentlemen in this trying time.) Tj T*
(One newspaper even went so far as to cease the publication of a) Tj T*
(remunerative page of small advertisements having to do with dealings) Tj T*
(in outside securities. This was done at the request of the Committee) Tj T*
(without hesitation. Others coöperated in the suppression of) Tj T*
(advertising on the part of questionable people, while correspondents) Tj T*
(of out of town newspapers, both foreign and domestic, cheerfully) Tj T*
(acceded to requests to suppress all disturbing financial reports. In a) Tj T*
(word, the financial department of the whole newspaper press accepted) Tj T*
(the situation philosophically, bearing their losses without complaint) Tj T*
(and supporting without cavil the restrictive measures which it was) Tj T*
(necessary to employ.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This loyal conduct of the press and of the auctioneers was one of the) Tj T*
(great factors without which the critical days of the suspension of) Tj T*
(business could not have been successfully surmounted.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(       *       *       *       *       *) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It will be remembered that in the morning of July 31st, the Governing) Tj T*
(Committee not only voted to close the Exchange but also declared that) Tj T*
(the delivery of securities should be suspended until further notice.) Tj T*
(The motive of this latter action was to prevent the possible) Tj T*
(insolvencies that were likely to be forced if purchasers were) Tj T*
(compelled to pay for their securities in the absence of a call money) Tj T*
(market. At the earliest moment that attention could be given to it the) Tj T*
(Committee of Five requested the Chairman of the Stock Exchange) Tj T*
(Clearing House to place before it the exact figures of the outstanding) Tj T*
(contracts. These figures when presented showed that there were stock) Tj T*
(balances open on Clearing House order amounting to $38,700,000 and) Tj T*
(Ex-Clearing House contracts amounting to about $61,000,000. Roughly) Tj T*
(speaking there had been about $100,000,000 of stock sold in the) Tj T*
(Exchange on July 30th, the delivery of which to the purchasers had) Tj T*
(been suspended by the action of the Governing Committee. Obviously a) Tj T*
(first great step toward clearing up the situation and preparing the) Tj T*
(ground for the ultimate reopening of the market was to get this great) Tj T*
(volume of contracts settled, so that if any failures were inevitable) Tj T*
(they would be disposed of beforehand.) Tj T*
