(When the Exchange suddenly closed its doors, an immense number of) Tj T*
(people, consisting of employees of the Exchange itself and the) Tj T*
(clerical forces of all the many brokerage houses, were rendered idle.) Tj T*
(As soon as it became evident that the suspension of business was going) Tj T*
(to be indefinitely prolonged, the grave question arose as to the) Tj T*
(extent to which these people would be thrown out of employment. The) Tj T*
(Stock Exchange at once set the generous example of deciding to retain) Tj T*
(its entire force without reduction of wages, and this decision was) Tj T*
(carried through for the entire four and one half months of suspension.) Tj T*
(A more difficult problem, however, confronted the brokerage houses.) Tj T*
(Many of these firms had very heavy office rents and fixed charges of) Tj T*
(various kinds; their business had been showing meager profits and even) Tj T*
(losses for some years and, the length of the period of closing being) Tj T*
(impossible to forecast, they did not dare to undertake burdens that) Tj T*
(might get them into difficulties. The result was that a few strong) Tj T*
(houses, with philanthropic proclivities, carried their clerical forces) Tj T*
(through on full pay, but the majority were obliged to cut them down in) Tj T*
(various ways. In some cases the full force was retained on greatly) Tj T*
(reduced salaries, in others salaries were reduced and part of the) Tj T*
(force discharged, and the net result was that a great number of) Tj T*
(unfortunates were either thrown into unemployment altogether or placed) Tj T*
(in very straightened circumstances.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is an interesting fact, bearing on the popular superstition that) Tj T*
(Wall Street is peopled by unprincipled worshippers of the dollar who) Tj T*
(are incapable of those finer qualities of character which are confined) Tj T*
(exclusively to other walks of life, that there is no region in which a) Tj T*
(quicker response to the call of the needy can be obtained than on the) Tj T*
(floor of the Stock Exchange. Even though the brokers were facing an) Tj T*
(indefinite period of starvation themselves, with expenses running on) Tj T*
(one side and receipts cut off on the other, the moment it became clear) Tj T*
(that severe suffering had come upon the clerical forces of the Street) Tj T*
(a movement was at once set on foot to start measures of relief and) Tj T*
(assistance. Perhaps the best way to convey an idea of the form which) Tj T*
(this assistance took is to quote from a report on the subject made by) Tj T*
