() Tj T*
(CHAPTER III) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE REOPENING OF THE EXCHANGE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The fact that the Stock Exchange closed on July 31st and did not) Tj T*
(reopen fully until December 15th, might lead to the supposition that) Tj T*
(the question of reopening was not taken up before December. Far from) Tj T*
(this being the case, the truth is that reopening began to be discussed) Tj T*
(immediately after the institution was closed. Within twenty-four hours) Tj T*
(of the closing the minority, who had not been at first convinced of) Tj T*
(the wisdom of that action, joined with the majority in urgently) Tj T*
(advising that the Exchange be not reopened soon. All through the month) Tj T*
(of August a growing anxiety over the possibility of some hasty action) Tj T*
(by the Exchange authorities showed itself among brokers, bankers, and) Tj T*
(even some government officials. For this anxiety there was never any) Tj T*
(basis, because the officers of the Exchange having exceptional means) Tj T*
(of knowing what the dangers were, had no intention of assuming the) Tj T*
(immense responsibilities of re-establishing the market without the) Tj T*
(backing and approval of the entire banking fraternity. Gradually the) Tj T*
(excited solicitude about a premature reopening subsided as the) Tj T*
(ultra-conservative attitude of the Exchange was understood, and this) Tj T*
(was followed ere long by the first symptoms of agitation for the) Tj T*
(establishment of some form of restricted market.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As we have already shown the restraints of July 31st were relaxed one) Tj T*
(by one with the lapse of time. First a market at or above the closing) Tj T*
(prices was organized under the Committee on Clearing House; then) Tj T*
(Committees to facilitate trading in listed and unlisted bonds were) Tj T*
(formed; and finally a market was provided for unlisted stocks. All) Tj T*
(these devices, however, while they brought about readjustment and) Tj T*
(diminution of strain, did not constitute a reopening of the Stock) Tj T*
(Exchange, and the restoration of that great primary market, in some) Tj T*
(restricted way, became more and more a subject of public interest and) Tj T*
(concern.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As we have seen, the fundamental reason for closing the Exchange was) Tj T*
(that America, when the war broke out, was in debt to Europe, and that) Tj T*
(Europe was sure to enforce the immediate payment of that debt in order) Tj T*
(to put herself in funds to prosecute this greatest of all wars. To use) Tj T*
(an illustration popular in Wall Street at the time, there was to be an) Tj T*
(unexpected run on Uncle Sam's Bank and the Stock Exchange was the) Tj T*
(paying teller's window through which the money was to be drawn out, so) Tj T*
(the window was closed to gain time. How to reopen this window in such) Tj T*
(a way as not to pay out any more money to the foreign creditor than) Tj T*
(would suit our own convenience was the problem which soon began to) Tj T*
(agitate many ingenious minds. As time went on plans for performing) Tj T*
(this difficult feat poured in upon the Committee of Five in constantly) Tj T*
(increasing volume, and they were frequently accompanied by a request) Tj T*
(on the part of their authors that, when adopted, the credit for their) Tj T*
ET
