(sought by the Exchange. So this mighty tempest in a tea pot resulted) Tj T*
(from the excessive zeal of an outsider who while trying to pilot the) Tj T*
(Committee into safe waters succeeded in running it on a reef of his) Tj T*
(own creation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Immediately on ascertaining the true situation the following notice) Tj T*
(was sent out on Saturday:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     "The Special Committee of Five announces that having consummated) Tj T*
(     its plan for bond transactions on the Exchange under certain) Tj T*
(     specified restrictions, the same will, in accordance with the) Tj T*
(     Constitution of the Exchange, be submitted to the Governing) Tj T*
(     Committee at the regular meeting to be held on the 24th inst. If) Tj T*
(     the recommendations of the Special Committee are adopted by the) Tj T*
(     Governing Committee the plan will go into operation at an early) Tj T*
(     date.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Some of the newspapers having announced positively that this new move) Tj T*
(with regard to bonds would take place on Monday, the 23rd, they were) Tj T*
(very indignant that it should be postponed without supplying them with) Tj T*
(a good and sufficient reason. The Committee, on its part, feeling) Tj T*
(that it was undesirable to publish the details of an awkward) Tj T*
(misunderstanding with a public official, who would not want his name) Tj T*
(dragged into a matter that he had in no way concerned himself with,) Tj T*
(refused to furnish the reason. This at once let loose upon them those) Tj T*
(vials of reportorial wrath which, up to that time, they had been) Tj T*
(fortunate in escaping. One journal amicably stated that this incident) Tj T*
(merely emphasized a fact which had all along been obvious, namely that) Tj T*
(the Committee were, and had been from the start, totally incompetent) Tj T*
(to perform the task intrusted to them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(While a gentle shower of epithets fell upon their devoted heads the) Tj T*
(Committee proceeded with their work and, having obtained the necessary) Tj T*
(authority from the Governing Committee, they sent out the following) Tj T*
(ruling on November 24th:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     "That so much of rule No. 21 as applies to dealings in listed) Tj T*
(     bonds through the Clearing House be rescinded, to take effect at) Tj T*
(     the close of business on Friday, November 27th, 1914. Beginning) Tj T*
(     on Saturday, November 28, 1914, dealings in bonds listed on the) Tj T*
(     Exchange will be permitted on the floor of the Exchange between) Tj T*
(     the hours of ten and three o'clock each day except Saturday, when) Tj T*
(     dealings shall cease at twelve o'clock noon. Such dealings to be) Tj T*
(     under the supervision and regulation of the Committee, and to be) Tj T*
(     for 'cash' or 'regular way' only and not below the minimum prices) Tj T*
(     as authorized by the Committee from time to time. Transactions at) Tj T*
(     prices other than those allowed by the Committee, or in evasion) Tj T*
(     of the Committee's rules, are prohibited. All rules of the) Tj T*
(     Exchange governing delivery and default on contracts covered by) Tj T*
(     this resolution shall be in force on and after Saturday, November) Tj T*
(     28th, 1914, but the closing of contracts 'under the rule' shall) Tj T*
(     be subject to the foregoing provisions.") Tj T*
ET
