(     "Loans of stocks _not_ admitted to dealings on the Exchange will) Tj T*
(     continue to stand until further notice, unless otherwise agreed) Tj T*
(     to by both parties to the contract.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On Monday, December 14th, the next business day after the limited list) Tj T*
(of stocks had been placed upon the floor of the Exchange, it was) Tj T*
(reported to the Committee that the volume of transactions taking place) Tj T*
(in the Stock Exchange Clearing House, in the stocks not yet admitted) Tj T*
(to the floor, had risen to such proportions as seriously to embarrass) Tj T*
(that institution. As this activity was taking place on a rising market) Tj T*
(and signs of increasing confidence were constantly multiplying, the) Tj T*
(Committee quickly resolved, on the same day, to transfer all stocks to) Tj T*
(the floor on the following morning, and notice to that effect was at) Tj T*
(once sent out. The unexpected appearance of this notice on the tape) Tj T*
(was greeted with cheers of approbation in the Exchange, and on) Tj T*
(December 15th the long hoped for reopening of the entire market had) Tj T*
(become a reality.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(       *       *       *       *       *) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Committee of Five by this act brought their own rule to a close.) Tj T*
(Arbitrary power had been put in their hands to be exercised while the) Tj T*
(Exchange remained closed, but now that it was reopened authority) Tj T*
(naturally returned to its legitimate channels. The Committee therefore) Tj T*
(presented the following report to the Governing Committee on December) Tj T*
(15th:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     "The Special Committee of Five beg leave to report that in as) Tj T*
(     much as the crisis that existed on July 31st, 1914, has passed,) Tj T*
(     and financial affairs in this country have resumed a practically) Tj T*
(     normal condition, the necessity for the Committee's continuance) Tj T*
(     no longer exists and hence they request to be discharged. Before) Tj T*
(     being discharged they desire to express their appreciation of the) Tj T*
(     trust and confidence placed in them by the Governing Committee.) Tj T*
(     They also wish to express to the members of the Exchange their) Tj T*
(     appreciation of the manner in which their rulings have been) Tj T*
(     respected, even though in many cases it involved great) Tj T*
(     sacrifices.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     Resolved, That the report of the Special Committee of Five be) Tj T*
(     received, and the Committee be discharged.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Thus, like the sudden and unexpected shifting of a dream, the) Tj T*
(Committee of Five who so recently had almost despaired of fixing a) Tj T*
(date for reopening the Exchange, found the Exchange open and) Tj T*
(themselves a memory of the past. The abruptness of their exit was) Tj T*
(tempered, however, in the following manner. As above described, the) Tj T*
(reopening was accompanied by the restraint of certain arbitrary) Tj T*
(minimum prices below which securities could not be sold. It was felt) Tj T*
(that, owing to the critical and indecisive state of the war, there was) Tj T*
(a continuing possibility of some news that might renew a crisis in the) Tj T*
